  "result": "Fixed! The bug was in the `wouldExceedLimit` call at line 50 of `project-service.ts`. \n\nBy passing `0` as the `requested` parameter, it was checking `used + 0 > limit` (i.e., is current usage already over?) instead of `used + 1 > limit` (i.e., would adding one more exceed?). This allowed organizations to create one extra project before being blocked.\n\nRemoving the explicit `0` parameter lets it default to `1`, which correctly checks whether adding one more project would exceed the quota. All tests now pass.",
